      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "While omeprazole can offer some protection against NSAID-induced stomach irritation, it is not a guaranteed shield and should not be relied upon when you are already experiencing acute symptoms like gnawing and soreness. Taking ibuprofen may still aggravate your stomach, potentially worsening your current condition before you can reach a doctor for a proper diagnosis. Given that over-the-counter relief isn't holding the pain down and your stomach is already compromised, waiting a few days out could risk a more serious infection or severe gastrointestinal complications.",
